<title>FRANCE: Axa says up to Suez board to decide merger.</title>
<headline>Axa says up to Suez board to decide merger.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Claude Bebear, head of insurer Axa-UAP, thinks it is up to the board of Cie de Suez to decide on its planned merger with Lyonnaise des Eaux and does not want to influence it, an Axa spokeswoman said on Thursday.</p>
<p>She had been asked for comment on a declaration by Saint-Gobain head Jean-Louis Beffa on Tuesday that Saint-Gobain, and other Suez shareholders, including Axa and Banque Nationale de Paris, were seeking a special dividend payout ahead of the merger.</p>
<p>&quot;He (Bebear) does not want to influence the decision of the Suez board, which must take this decision completely calmly,&quot; the spokeswoman said.</p>
</text>
